# Networking map I must know

I previously used "networking" too broadly, so enforce this model:

```text
Application integration logic
  - sync semantics
  - normalization
  - retries
  - idempotency
  - provider adapters
        |
API protocol
  - REST/JSON/webhooks
  - HTTP methods/status codes
        |
Security/session
  - API keys/OAuth
  - TLS identity
        |
Transport/network
  - DNS
  - TCP
  - routing/firewalls/proxies
```

Examples:

`401 Unauthorized`
Usually application authentication, not "the network is down."

`429 Too Many Requests`
Provider/application rate limit.

`504 Gateway Timeout`
A gateway did not get a timely upstream response.

DNS resolution failure
Networking/name-resolution layer.

TLS certificate verification error
Secure transport/identity layer.

Connection timeout
Could be network path, firewall, unreachable service, overloaded endpoint, etc.

Read timeout
Connection exists, but response did not arrive within the configured time.

Make me diagnose the layer before proposing a fix.

