# Interview debugging drills

Regularly give me one of these with incomplete evidence.

## Drill A
Customer: "Employee updates stopped yesterday."

Give me logs one clue at a time.
Do not reveal root cause until I form a debugging plan.

Possible causes:
- expired credentials,
- revoked scopes,
- provider outage,
- 429,
- webhook stopped,
- poll checkpoint bug,
- schema drift,
- normalization error,
- queue backlog.

## Drill B
Only one provider is failing for all customers.

Make me reason about blast radius.

## Drill C
Only one customer is failing across an otherwise healthy provider.

Make me focus on account-specific auth/config/data.

## Drill D
Writes sometimes create duplicates.

Make me reason about timeout ambiguity + idempotency.

## Drill E
Data appears 20 minutes late.

Make me distinguish:
- provider freshness,
- sync cadence,
- queue delay,
- webhook delay,
- customer pull behavior.

